cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use peabiru, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "peabiru: multimodal routing on OpenStreetMap and GTFS networks"
abstract: >-
  peabiru computes travel-time matrices and accessibility on multimodal
  transport networks (walk, bicycle, car and public transport) built from
  OpenStreetMap extracts and GTFS feeds. Its routing engine is a Rust port of
  Conveyal's R5 and needs no Java runtime. The same engine is distributed as the Rust crate
  peabiru-core and as the R and Python packages peabiru.
